      "answer": "The paper reports the following data sizes: the Visual Genome (VG) training set consists of 85% of the data — 16k images with 740k corresponding region descriptions — while the ReferIt training data consists of 9k images and 54k referring expressions [6]. In addition, the instance selection model is trained using (region description, object set) pairs from the VG dataset, resulting in a training set of approximately 1.73M samples, with the remaining 300K samples split into validation and testing [4]. The instance selection covers 2,909 instance classes [1].",
      "insufficient": false,
      "citations": [
